(Binary favicon.ico file - This is a placeholder comment)

NOTE: The favicon.ico should be generated from the favicon.svg above.
You can use online tools or image editors to convert the SVG to ICO format.

For GitHub Pages deployment, the SVG favicon will work in modern browsers.
The ICO serves as a fallback for older browsers.

Recommended approach:
1. Use the favicon.svg as the primary favicon (already linked in index.html)
2. Generate a 32x32 ICO from the SVG using a tool like:
   - https://convertio.co/svg-ico/
   - https://cloudconvert.com/svg-to-ico
   - OR use a design tool like Figma/Illustrator to export

For now, the SVG favicon will function correctly in all modern browsers.
